From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: odroid-go-ultra: PMIC buses at 400 kHz in U-Boot

U-Boot probes the RK817's and RK818's regulators register by register
before the display and the storage; at the default 100 kHz that was
~140 ms. Both PMICs take fast mode (400 kHz). Linux keeps its own setting.

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
index 1a06c5ca678..4cdf70cd3b8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -85,3 +85,16 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm_f_h_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The two PMICs at 400 kHz instead of the default 100 kHz (RK817 and
+ * RK818: fast mode): U-Boot probes their regulators one register at a
+ * time before the display and the storage.
+ */
+&i2c_AO {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+};
+
+&i2c3 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+};
